# M1 exit transcript (ARCHITECTURE §22.3, WP 1.26)

`vertical_slice.in/vertical_slice.py` holds the 19 statements of the M1 exit transcript, both
syntaxes mixed: clear the factory scene, add a cylinder, give it a metallic `Steel` material,
add a camera, render it with Workbench, export a GLB, save a `.frap`, start empty, import the
GLB back (its material is still metallic), reopen the `.frap` (the cylinder is where it was).
Output paths are cwd-relative (`out/…`, never `//`, §17.2); the sandbox starts empty.

The same statements run in the other two transports:

- `vertical_slice_stdin.toml`: raw mode, statements on stdin (§13.1);
- `vertical_slice_serve.toml`: `frap serve --jsonl`, one request per statement, so the session
  state crosses requests (§13.1, §13.5).

Every statement must finish (`"ok":true`). The values that prove the round trips are pinned
(the imported `Metallic` is `1`, the reopened cylinder is at `[0,0,1]`); the rest of each
response (the `result` of render/export/import, `changes`, `context`) is elided with `[..]` so
that the exit criterion does not freeze details owned by the operator WPs (1.20, 1.23, 1.24),
which have their own goldens and transcripts. The render needs a GPU adapter (Metal, lavapipe,
WARP on the CI matrix).

The error-code section below runs first, so that a failing exit transcript does not hide it
(trycmd skips the remaining steps of a file after a failure).

## Error codes (runs first)

The golden cases under `tests/golden/cases/{errors,rna,context,poll}/` compare every error's
exception class and message with Blender 5.2.4 (fixtures blessed from Blender); goldens do not
see frap's `code`. `vertical_slice.in/error_codes.py` raises each M1-reachable code once so
that the code, span, detail and hint are pinned too, including the frap-only codes Blender has
no counterpart for (`UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX`, `OP_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`, `NOT_IMPLEMENTED`,
`OP_ARG_POSITIONAL` D-01, `ZERO_DIVISION` D-25, `RNA_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`, `IO_ERROR`,
`LIMIT_EXCEEDED`). `REQUEST_INVALID` and `DESCRIBE_TARGET` are pinned by the WP 1.25
transcripts under `cli/`; `RNA_EDITMODE_WRITE` needs Edit Mode (M2); `GPU_UNAVAILABLE` needs a
build without `gpu`. (snapbox turns backslashes into `/`, so `\"` reads `/"` below.)

